1. Generate More Authentic Reviews at Every Location
A multi-location review request has two jobs. It must reach the customer at a sensible moment, and it must connect that customer with the correct location. Strong programs also make the request feel relevant to the actual interaction so the customer has an easier starting point for writing.

Standardize the system while personalizing the request
Corporate teams should standardize the channel options, permitted fields, follow-up cadence, location routing, opt-out handling, and measurement. They should also maintain approved corporate and brand messages while each location maintains accurate local details. The request can draw on this knowledge along with customer and service context such as the location, date, product, service, employee, milestone, or completed-work photo. A short neutral question can help the customer recall useful detail without telling the customer what opinion to express.

