Set approval rules around consequence, not convenience
Low-risk positive reviews may be eligible for automatic publishing after the same quality checks. Reviews involving complaints, privacy, rating-text mismatches, named employees, legal language, safety, discrimination, or unclear facts should route to a person. The goal is to involve the right person when the response carries real consequence. Every review type can benefit from relevant knowledge. The system should vary how it uses that knowledge based on the review, the location, and the risk.

